[ContentType "Intro"]
[White "Chapter"]
[Black "Introduction"]
[Result "*"]

{After  1. d4  ♘f6  2. c4  g6  3. ♘c3  ♗g7  4. e4  d6  5. h3  O-O  6. ♗e3 Black's second most popular option is 6... c5 .          ♖♘♗♕⨯♖♔⨯         ♙♙⨯⨯♙♙♗♙         ⨯⨯⨯♙⨯♘♙⨯         ⨯⨯♙⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯♙♙♙⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯♘⨯♗⨯⨯♙         ♙♙⨯⨯⨯♙♙⨯         ♖⨯⨯♕♔♗♘♖     White has three good moves to choose from, depending on their style and taste:  7. ♘f3 , 7. d5 and 7. dxc5 .    In this chapter, we examine the first option, which typically leads to a Maroczy-like structure with the rather unusual inclusion of h2-h3 instead of f2-f3.  }

