{ 1. d4  ♘f6  2. c4  g6  3. ♘c3  ♗g7  4. e4  d6  5. h3  O-O  6. ♗e3  c5   Now let's look at 7. d5 , which is arguably more in the spirit of the system than the other two options.           ♖♘♗♕⨯♖♔⨯         ♙♙⨯⨯♙♙♗♙         ⨯⨯⨯♙⨯♘♙⨯         ⨯⨯♙♙⨯⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯♙⨯♙⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯♘⨯♗⨯⨯♙         ♙♙⨯⨯⨯♙♙⨯         ♖⨯⨯♕♔♗♘♖     Black can choose Benko Gambit style play with  7...b5  8. cxb5  a6 , or  7...e6  followed by  e6xd5 , after which White may steer the game into Modern Benoni territory with c4xd5, or into a symmetrical King's Indian structure with e4xd5.  }

