{ 1. d4  ♘f6  2. c4  g6  3. ♘c3  ♗g7  4. e4  d6  5. h3  O-O  6. ♗e3           ♖♘♗♕⨯♖♔⨯         ♙♙♙⨯♙♙♗♙         ⨯⨯⨯♙⨯♘♙⨯         ⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯♙♙♙⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯♘⨯♗⨯⨯♙         ♙♙⨯⨯⨯♙♙⨯         ♖⨯⨯♕♔♗♘♖     There are a few responses other than 6...e5 or 6...c5 that Black can try, most notably  6...♘a6 .  Often these lines transpose to variations considered earlier.   The line that does not transpose is 6...♘c6 . Black is hoping for  7. ♘f3  e5  8. d5  ♘d4           ♖⨯♗♕⨯♖♔⨯         ♙♙♙⨯⨯♙♗♙         ⨯⨯⨯♙⨯♘♙⨯         ⨯⨯⨯♙♙⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯♙♘♙⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯♘⨯♗♘⨯♙         ♙♙⨯⨯⨯♙♙⨯         ♖⨯⨯♕♔♗⨯♖     with equality. However, White can instead respond with 7.d5, reaching a favourable position.  }

