 {[%eval +0.28]}  *

[Guid "R21e5e54ba38848959b5c9fdac62543a0"]
[ContentType "Intro"]
[White "Chapter"]
[Black "Introduction"]
[Result "*"]

{This chapter contains fragments of blitz games played at a relatively modest level, by players rated roughly 2000 to 2200 on Lichess.org and Chess.com.  The idea is that such games are full of strategic and tactical mistakes, though usually not simple one-move blunders. When explained, these mistakes can help lower-rated players understand the nuances of the opening. Such nuances often remain hidden in games played at master and, of course, grandmaster level.  Ideally, these examples would come from classical games rather than blitz games. Unfortunately, the availability of classical games at this level in the databases is very limited, while there are plenty of online blitz games. }

