 {[%eval +0.35]}  *

[Guid "R01a036ab39754af1867bbbd3bc4784a1"]
[ContentType "Intro"]
[White "Chapter"]
[Black "Introduction"]
[Result "*"]

{This chapter presents a collection of positions in which a white pawn has already advanced to g5 when Black launches the typical counterattack in the centre with  f7-f5.          ⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯♙         ⨯⨯⨯♙⨯⨯♙⨯         ⨯⨯⨯♙♙♙♙⨯         ⨯⨯♙⨯♙⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯         ⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯⨯     White has a choice between the “simple” capture  e4xf5 , the en passant capture g5xf6, or keeping the tension and making another move.   The nuances of each particular position determine which option is best. Understanding these strategic and tactical subtleties is essential to understanding the opening as a whole.  }

